---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Company policies — M3MM"
  description="M3MM company policies covering workplace vaccination, accessibility, and how policy updates are published."
  path="/policies"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'M3MM', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Company policies', url: '/policies' },
  ]}
>
  <Header slot="header" minimal={true} path="/policies" />

  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden py-hq-section">

    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="grid h-12 w-12 flex-none place-items-center overflow-hidden bg-ink-soft ring-1 ring-ink-line" style="border-radius: 2px;">
          <img src="/mark-light.png" alt="M3MM" width="38" height="38" class="h-9 w-9 object-contain" decoding="async" />
        </span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker mono">M3MM · Policy library</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.17em] text-bone-muted">Modernize. Mobilize. Multiply.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h1 class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-hq-hero">
        Company policies,<br />
        <span class="text-bone-dim">written in plain English.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
        The rules M3MM has formally adopted are published here so employees, contractors,
        applicants, clients, and visitors know what to expect.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[240px,minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
        <aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 lg:h-fit" aria-label="Policy index">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-bone-muted">Policy index</p>
          <nav class="mt-4 border-l border-ink-line" aria-label="Company policies">
            <a href="#covid-vaccination" data-cta="policies-jump-vaccination" data-section="policies" data-intent="product:company-policies" class="block border-l border-clay py-2 pl-4 text-sm text-bone transition-colors hover:text-clay">COVID-19 vaccination</a>
            <a href="#accessibility" data-cta="policies-jump-accessibility" data-section="policies" data-intent="product:company-policies" class="block py-2 pl-4 text-sm text-bone-dim transition-colors hover:text-bone">Accessibility</a>
            <a href="#updates" data-cta="policies-jump-updates" data-section="policies" data-intent="product:company-policies" class="block py-2 pl-4 text-sm text-bone-dim transition-colors hover:text-bone">Updates and scope</a>
          </nav>
        </aside>

        <div class="space-y-10">
          <article id="covid-vaccination" class="panel relative overflow-hidden p-6 sm:p-9" aria-labelledby="covid-policy-heading">
            <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-clay to-transparent"></div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-ink-line pb-5">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-clay">Adopted policy</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-bone-muted">Effective · August 18, 2026</span>
            </div>

            <h2 id="covid-policy-heading" class="mt-7 font-display text-3xl text-bone sm:text-4xl">COVID-19 vaccination</h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
              M3MM does not require COVID-19 vaccination as a condition of employment,
              contract work, or participation in company activities. Vaccination is a personal
              choice. M3MM will not penalize or treat someone differently solely because they
              choose not to receive a COVID-19 vaccine.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-7 border-l-2 border-clay bg-ink-soft/50 px-5 py-4">
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-bone-muted">Definition</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
                For this policy, “vaccination” refers to full vaccination against COVID-19, the
                disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <section>
                <h3 class="font-medium text-bone">Medical privacy</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
                  M3MM will not request vaccination records unless applicable law or a
                  client-controlled worksite requires them. Any information collected for that
                  limited purpose will be handled as confidential medical information.
                </p>
              </section>
              <section>
                <h3 class="font-medium text-bone">Client and site requirements</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
                  A client-controlled location may set its own lawful health requirements. When
                  that happens, M3MM will consider practical alternatives such as remote work,
                  remote participation, or reassignment.
                </p>
              </section>
              <section>
                <h3 class="font-medium text-bone">Respect and non-retaliation</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
                  Personal medical decisions must be treated respectfully. Retaliation,
                  harassment, or pressure based on vaccination status is not part of M3MM’s
                  workplace culture.
                </p>
              </section>
              <section>
                <h3 class="font-medium text-bone">When someone is sick</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
                  Anyone experiencing symptoms of a contagious illness should avoid in-person
                  work and use remote-work options when practical, regardless of vaccination status.
                </p>
              </section>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 border-t border-ink-line pt-6 text-xs leading-relaxed text-bone-muted">
              <p>
                Reference guidance:
                <a data-cta="policies-osha" data-section="policies" data-intent="product:company-policies" href="https://www.osha.gov/common-respiratory-illnesses/general-recommendations" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-clay underline decoration-clay/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-bone">OSHA workplace recommendations</a>
                and
                <a data-cta="policies-eeoc" data-section="policies" data-intent="product:company-policies" href="https://www.eeoc.gov/federal-laws-protect-you-against-employment-discrimination-during-covid-19-pandemic" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-clay underline decoration-clay/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-bone">EEOC employment guidance</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <section id="accessibility" class="panel p-6 sm:p-9" aria-labelledby="accessibility-policy-heading">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-clay">Public commitment</p>
            <h2 id="accessibility-policy-heading" class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl text-bone">Accessibility</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
              M3MM aims to make its website usable by as many people as possible, including
              people with disabilities. The full statement documents the current standard,
              completed work, known limits, and contact path.
            </p>
            <a href="/accessibility" class="mt-6 inline-flex text-sm text-clay underline decoration-clay/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-bone" data-cta="policies-accessibility" data-section="policies">Read the accessibility statement →</a>
          </section>

          <section id="updates" class="border-t border-ink-line pt-8" aria-labelledby="updates-heading">
            <h2 id="updates-heading" class="font-display text-2xl text-bone">Updates and scope</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-bone-dim">
              M3MM will add policies here as the company grows and new requirements are formally
              adopted. The effective date shown on each policy controls. Applicable law and valid
              contractual requirements take priority where they conflict with a published policy.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-bone-muted">Page last updated · August 18, 2026</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" path="/policies" />
</Layout>
